x86_64-windows  Refused before it reaches the question it asks, and by an older refusal: a class-typed throw needs the Microsoft ThrowInfo chain pointed at a class - a type descriptor and a catchable type per class, and a _CTA array listing the thrown class and its bases - and cxx1 emits those four objects for a fundamental type only. throw-class.notarget records the same lag at length. Everything this case measures is the Itanium path in any event: there is no `__cxa_end_catch` on that ABI, a handler being a funclet the runtime ends the catch for when it returns. What this target does with the jumps themselves is refuse them by name - `return`, and now `break` and `continue`, out of a handler, all three for the same reason: leaving a funclet early means handing back the address to carry on at in the register a return value would travel in, which is not built. try-catch.notarget records that from the other side.
